    "sections" : [
      {
        "executes" : true,
        "heading" : "When to invoke",
        "line" : 21,
        "lines" : [
          "\"orchestrate pipeline dag\"",
          "\"run dag orchestration\"",
          "\"run the dag orchestration pass\""
        ],
        "role" : "applicability"
      },
      {
        "executes" : true,
        "heading" : "Workflow",
        "line" : 26,
        "lines" : [
          "fetch datasets",
          "for each dataset:",
          "wait for event upstream.done matching the event's dataset name equals the dataset's name",
          "wait for signal \"pipeline.ready\"",
          "simultaneously:",
          "extract a dataset from the object store source",
          "run quality checks on the dataset",
          "Emit: \"dag orchestration pass complete\""
        ],
        "role" : "procedure"
      },
      {
        "executes" : false,
        "heading" : "Anti-Patterns",
        "line" : 36,
        "lines" : [
          "Don't remove the `pipeline.ready` wait to shave latency. The upstream",
          "completion event only proves the upstream is done; it doesn't prove the",
          "orchestrator has cleared this stage to start",
          "Don't run the extraction and the quality check sequentially \"to be safe.\"",
          "They're independent once both gates clear — running them one after the",
          "other only adds latency without adding safety"
        ],
        "role" : "reference"
      },
      {
        "executes" : false,
        "heading" : "Report shape",
        "line" : 44,
        "lines" : [
          "The receipt confirms each dataset's upstream signal and downstream",
          "extraction, so a pipeline engineer can see exactly where a stage was",
          "waiting versus where it was actually running"
        ],
        "role" : "template"
      }
    ],
    "triggers" : "\"orchestrate pipeline dag\"\n\"run dag orchestration\"\n\"run the dag orchestration pass\""
